FPC-SAFESEH 2
# Reviewed input identities for the supplied FPC 3.3.1+7 Win32 units.
# Hashes cover whole objects, including registrations through pointer stores.
# Only linked objects are required and hashed. A new unit must be audited.
# handler = OS SEH entry; nonseh = reviewed ordinary function/callback.
# A handler may be absent only with an explicit Removing object(section) map record.
#
# Audited against the reviewed 3.2.4-rc2+1 inputs (fpc-3.2.4.manifest, before
# this file replaced it), object by object with objdump -dr: the same objects
# plus rtl/sortbase.o, which 3.3.1 links for list sorting and which installs
# only a compiler-generated __FPC_finally_handler frame. Across all of them the
# same nine routines write FS outside a compiler-generated frame (system.o's
# main_wrapper, exe_entry, fpc_leave, fpc_doneexception, fpc_longjmp and
# fpc_safecallhandler; signals.o's install_exception_handler,
# remove_exception_handler and jumptohandlesignal), in the same shapes, and
# the same handler symbols are referenced. seh32.inc's changes since 3.2.4
# keep exception objects on their own list and save registers around
# RtlUnwind; NestedHandler stays the only frame replacement. 3.3.1 mangles a
# hashed name as $h... where 3.2.4 used $crc..., which renames sections here
# but not the routines. rtti.o's TSystemFunctionCallback.Handler (the target
# of its call thunks) and CallHandler methods are now linked: ordinary code.
#
# 3.3.1+7 (patches 0129 to 0134: the SLP optimizer and aarch64 branches): each
# object below hashes the same as in 3.3.1+6, so the 3.3.1+6 audit holds.
#
# 3.3.1+8 (patches 0135 to 0141): only rtl/system.o changed. Compared with
# 3.3.1+7 by objdump -dr: LinkExceptEntry's last parameter is now a Boolean and
# it stores the exception object's own address or nil in that object's field
# (+0x18); __FPC_DEFAULT_HANDLER and CommonHandler pass it a constant. No
# changed routine touches FS, the FS accesses are the same section by section,
# and the handler symbols referenced are the same, so the audit holds.
#
# 3.3.1+9 (patches 0142 and 0143: an inlined function's MM-register result):
# each object below hashes the same as in 3.3.1+8, so the 3.3.1+8 audit holds.
version 3.3.1+9
target i386-win32

